ardy-mlx
Copyright 2026 gmgn radio contributors

An independent MLX (Apple Silicon) implementation of the motion model from:

  ARDY — "Autoregressive Diffusion with Hybrid Representation for Interactive
  Human Motion Generation", NVIDIA (nv-tlabs/ardy, SIGGRAPH 2026).
  Source code: Apache License 2.0.  Checkpoints: per-model terms (see below).

Policy (same as the sibling project motionbrick-mlx):
* We take the SOURCE-CODE route only. Reference source is Apache-2.0.
* Checkpoints carry their OWN terms per model. Those terms have now been read
  and recorded in docs/decisions/0002-checkpoint-terms.md (NVIDIA Open Model
  License, 2025-10-24): local inference, format conversion, fine-tuning and
  commercial use are permitted; redistribution is permitted subject to
  attaching the agreement and the attribution notice. The agreement is
  revocable and terminates if guardrails are circumvented. We do not
  redistribute NVIDIA weights or golden outputs derived from them.
* Reference runs happen on a Linux/CUDA box we do not own; that box stays
  read-only and is used as a golden-output oracle only.
